              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="slide" data-slide="4" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="copy">
            <p class="kicker">What that changed</p>
            <h3>HERA stops being &ldquo;better chat&rdquo;</h3>
            <p>
              Rough intent &rarr; structured work &rarr; human only when genuinely needed.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

      </div>

      <!-- next arrow for slides 2-4 only; slide 1 has its own arrow inside slide1-wrapper -->
      <button class="nav-arrow next" type="button" data-next aria-label="Next idea" hidden>→</button>

      <div class="footer">
        <span data-count>1 / 5</span>
        <div class="dots" aria-label="Choose a story slide">
          <button class="active" type="button" data-dot="0" aria-label="Show slide 1" aria-current="true"></button>
          <button type="button" data-dot="1" aria-label="Show slide 2"></button>
          <button type="button" data-dot="2" aria-label="Show slide 3"></button>
          <button type="button" data-dot="3" aria-label="Show slide 4"></button>
          <button type="button" data-dot="4" aria-label="Show slide 5"></button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="outro" data-outro aria-hidden="true">
      <p>
        That is usually how I work: I follow the friction until I can describe the burden
        <strong>the user should never have been carrying in the first place.</strong>
      </p>
    </div>
